{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "339836968",
    "title": "1. Catalog & Product Setup",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339836968",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 3,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nThis checklist covers catalog and product configuration in Salesforce Business Manager. Correct catalog structure is foundational — errors here silently break PDPs, navigation, and internationalisation across all seven Zimmermann storefronts.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Reference:** [Check the Products and Catalogs Setup — Trailhead](https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/b2c-solution-functional-launch-readiness/b2c-review-business-manager)\n\n**⚠️ Risk note:** A departing SFCC architect may hold catalog structure decisions in their head. Run this checklist against each of the seven sites (AU, UK, US Domestic, US Intl, EU Domestic, EU Intl, ME) and record findings.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### Catalog Structure\n\nincompleteA **product catalog** exists and owns all master products\nincompleteA **storefront catalog** exists per site — products are assigned (not owned) within it\nincompleteThe storefront catalog is correctly assigned to each site in BM\nincompleteCategory tree in the storefront catalog mirrors the intended site navigation\nincompleteStorefront catalog is configured independently per site to support locale-specific navigation\n\n### Product Data\n\nincompleteAll variation attributes are defined and mapped correctly (size, colour, etc.)\nincompleteImage viewtype mappings are correct (wrong mappings silently break PDP image galleries)\nincompleteVariation attribute display names are set correctly per locale\nincompleteCustom product attributes from the agreed data model are mapped and populated in BM\n\n### Cleanup\n\nincompleteRefArch / demo attributes removed from product attribute groups\nincompleteRefArch / demo attributes removed from category attribute groups\nincompleteNo test/placeholder products are visible on any storefront\n\n### Per-Site Verification (repeat for each storefront)\n\nincompleteAU — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteUK — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteUS Domestic — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteUS Intl — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteEU Domestic — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteEU Intl — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\nincompleteME — storefront catalog assigned and category tree verified\n\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4e6",
    "page_width": "full-width"
  }
}"}

