      "value": "This page documents the alternative catalogue sync design using **SCAPI Admin APIs** instead of WebDAV file-based import. It covers the same three data domains — Product, Price, and Inventory — and follows the same section structure as the file-based design for direct comparison.\n\n> **Context:** The file-based design (WebDAV + import job) is the recommended approach for Zimmermann's catalogue scale. This SCAPI Admin API design is documented as the alternative pattern — applicable for real-time single-product event scenarios or if the file-based approach is ruled out. See the [parent page comparison](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418) for the full pro/con trade-off.\n\nRelated pages: - [TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price & Inventory (MuleSoft → SFCC)](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418) — file-based design - [TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292061208) - [TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345) - [TSD: Price — SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292388871)\n\n---\n\n1-overview1. Overview\n---------------------\n\nIn the SCAPI Admin API pattern, MuleSoft calls SFCC REST endpoints directly per product or inventory record. Each domain uses a dedicated SCAPI Admin API family.\n\n> **API Note:** OCAPI is deprecated. All SFCC Admin API calls use **SCAPI Admin APIs** authenticated via **Account Manager OAuth2 (AmOAuth2)** — client credentials grant.\n>\n> ⚠️ **Price sync exception:** There is no published SCAPI Admin API or verified OCAPI endpoint for writing pricebook entries programmatically. **Price sync must always use the file-based pricebook XML import** (WebDAV + `sfcc-site-archive-import` job) regardless of which pattern is chosen for products and inventory. See Section 5.\n\n| Domain | Mechanism | SCAPI API | Auth | API Reference |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Product | SCAPI Admin API (per product/variant) | Products Admin API — `POST` / `PUT` | AmOAuth2 | [Products](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/products) |\n| Price | **File-based only** — WebDAV + import job | No SCAPI API exists | AmOAuth2 (WebDAV) | — |\n| Inventory | SCAPI Admin API (per record) | Inventory Lists API — `PUT` / `PATCH` | AmOAuth2 | [Inventory Lists](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/inventory-lists) |\n\n**SCAPI Admin API base URL:**Defaultnonehttps://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com\n\n**Auth token acquisition (product and inventory domains):**DefaultnonePOST https://account.demandware.com/dwsso/oauth2/access\\_token\nContent-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\ngrant\\_type=client\\_credentials\n&client\\_id={mulesoftClientId}\n&client\\_secret={mulesoftClientSecret}\n\n---\n\n2-sequencing-constraints2. Sequencing Constraints\n-------------------------------------------------\n\nUnlike the file-based import job which handles sequencing internally, the SCAPI Admin API pattern requires MuleSoft to enforce strict operation order across product and inventory domains. Price sync runs independently via file-based import and does not participate in this sequence.\n\nDefaultnoneFor each style (master product):\nSTEP 1 — Create or update MASTER product\nPOST /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}\nSTEP 2 — Create or update each VARIANT\nPOST /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}\n⚠ Must complete after Step 1 — variant fails if master does not exist\nSTEP 3 — Assign products to CATEGORIES\nPUT /product/v1/.../categories/{categoryId}/products/{productId}\n⚠ Must complete after Step 1\nSTEP 4 — Write INVENTORY\nPUT /inventory/v1/.../inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}\n⚠ Must complete after Step 2 — variant must exist before inventory record\nSTEP 5 — PRICE SYNC (file-based — independent of above sequence)\nPricebook XML → WebDAV → sfcc-site-archive-import job\nRuns on its own schedule\n⚠ Variant must exist in SFCC before a pricebook entry for it is valid\n\n---\n\n3-sync-orchestration--mulesoft-flow-product-and-inventory3. Sync Orchestration — MuleSoft Flow (Product and Inventory)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe SCAPI Admin API pattern requires a **separate MuleSoft flow per domain** (product, inventory), each with its own retry logic, error tracking, and partial-success handling. Price sync uses the file-based flow documented in the [parent page](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418).\n\nDefaultnoneAP21 / NewStore (source event or scheduler trigger)\n│\n▼\nMuleSoft\n│\n├── 1. GET AmOAuth2 TOKEN\n│ POST https://account.demandware.com/dwsso/oauth2/access\\_token\n│ Cache token; refresh before expiry (typically 30 min TTL)\n│\n├── 2. CHECK PRODUCT EXISTS (product domain only)\n│ GET /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}/{productId}\n│ → 200: product exists → use PUT to update\n│ → 404: product does not exist → use POST to create\n│\n├── 3. EXECUTE API CALL\n│ POST / PUT per domain (see Sections 4 and 6)\n│ Headers: Authorization: Bearer {amOAuth2Token}\n│ Content-Type: application/json\n│ → 200 / 201: success\n│ → 4xx: business error — log, skip record, continue\n│ → 429: rate limit — back off and retry\n│ → 5xx: server error — retry up to 3 times with exponential back-off\n│\n├── 4. TRACK RESULT PER RECORD\n│ { productId: \"success\" | \"failed\" | \"skipped\" }\n│\n├── 5. CONTINUE TO NEXT RECORD\n│ Do not abort entire batch on a single record failure\n│\n└── 6. POST-RUN SUMMARY\nIf any records failed → raise alert via Anypoint monitoring\nStore failed record IDs for manual replay or next-run retry\n\n---\n\n4-product-sync4. Product Sync\n-----------------------------\n\n### 41-trigger4.1 Trigger\n\nAP21 product create or update event consumed by MuleSoft. Can be event-driven (real-time per product) or scheduled batch.\n\n### 42-api-endpoints4.2 API Endpoints\n\n| Operation | Method | Endpoint | When |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Create master | `POST` | `/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}` | Product does not exist |\n| Update master | `PUT` | `/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}/{productId}` | Product exists |\n| Create variant | `POST` | `/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}` | Variant does not exist — after master created |\n| Update variant | `PUT` | `/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}/{productId}` | Variant exists |\n| Assign to category | `PUT` | `/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/categories/{categoryId}/products/{productId}` | After product created |\n\n### 43-master-product-payload4.3 Master Product Payload\n\nDefaultjson{\n\"id\": \"4673TS251\",\n\"name\": { \"default\": \"Aster Fit & Flare Dress\" },\n\"longDescription\": { \"default\": \"...\" },\n\"online\": true,\n\"searchable\": true,\n\"taxClassId\": \"standard\",\n\"type\": { \"master\": true },\n\"variationAttributes\": [\n{\n\"id\": \"color\",\n\"name\": { \"default\": \"Colour\" },\n\"values\": [{ \"value\": \"GVSCP\", \"name\": { \"default\": \"Guava Seascape\" } }]\n},\n{ \"id\": \"size\", \"name\": { \"default\": \"Size\" } }\n],\n\"c\\_styleNumber\": \"4673TS251\",\n\"c\\_season\": \"SS25\",\n\"c\\_label\": \"Ready to Wear\",\n\"c\\_fabricComposition\": \"100% Silk\",\n\"c\\_careInstructions\": \"Dry clean only\",\n\"c\\_countryOfOrigin\": \"China\",\n\"c\\_isFinalSale\": false\n}\n\n### 44-variant-product-payload4.4 Variant Product Payload\n\nDefaultjson{\n\"id\": \"4673TS251GVSCP0P\",\n\"masterProductId\": \"4673TS251\",\n\"upc\": \"9312345678901\",\n\"online\": true,\n\"searchable\": false,\n\"type\": { \"variant\": true },\n\"variationValues\": { \"color\": \"GVSCP\", \"size\": \"0P\" },\n\"c\\_color\": \"GVSCP\",\n\"c\\_refinementColor\": \"Guava Seascape\",\n\"c\\_size\": \"0P\"\n}\n\n### 45-upsert-pattern4.5 Upsert Pattern\n\nSCAPI does not have a native upsert endpoint for products. MuleSoft must check existence before every write:\n\nDefaultnoneGET /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}/{productId}\n→ 200 → PUT (update)\n→ 404 → POST (create)\n\nFor a batch of 1,000 products × 5 variants = 12,000 API calls (6,000 existence checks + 6,000 writes).\n\n---\n\n5-price-sync--filebased-only5. Price Sync — File-Based Only\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\n> ⚠️ **No SCAPI Admin API exists for writing pricebook entries.**\n>\n> This has been confirmed against Salesforce developer documentation — no SCAPI Admin API for pricebook entry writes exists as a published endpoint. OCAPI is deprecated and must not be used for new integrations.\n>\n> **Price sync must use the file-based pricebook XML import regardless of which pattern is chosen for products and inventory.**\n\n### 51-mechanism5.1 Mechanism\n\nPricebook XML delivered via WebDAV + `sfcc-site-archive-import` job — identical to the file-based design. See [TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price & Inventory — Section 5](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418) for the full specification.\n\n### 52-scope5.2 Scope\n\nDomestic sites only — AU, UK, US, EU. International sites (USIntl, EUIntl, HK, ME) pricing is managed by Global-e.\n\n| Site | List Pricebook ID | Sale Pricebook ID |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `au-aud-list-prices` | `au-aud-sale-prices` |\n| ZimmermannUK | `uk-gbp-list-prices` | `uk-gbp-sale-prices` |\n| ZimmermannUS | `us-usd-list-prices` | `us-usd-sale-prices` |\n| ZimmermannEU | `eu-eur-list-prices` | `eu-eur-sale-prices` |\n\n### 53-implication-for-hybrid-pattern5.3 Implication for Hybrid Pattern\n\nIf Zimmermann selects SCAPI Admin API for product and inventory sync, MuleSoft must still implement the WebDAV + job-trigger flow for price sync. Both flows co-exist:\n\n* **Product + Inventory** → SCAPI Admin API per-record calls\n* **Price** → WebDAV pricebook XML + `sfcc-site-archive-import` job\n\n---\n\n6-inventory-sync6. Inventory Sync\n---------------------------------\n\n### 61-trigger6.1 Trigger\n\nEvery 15 minutes per region (AU, GB, US). EU, EUIntl, HK, ME coverage to be confirmed — see open item #3.\n\n### 62-source6.2 Source\n\nNewStore S3 availability export → MuleSoft decompresses and transforms to SCAPI Inventory Lists API payloads.\n\n### 63-api-reference6.3 API Reference\n\n[SCAPI Inventory Lists API](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/inventory-lists) — Admin API, AmOAuth2 auth.\n\n**Base path:**Defaultnonehttps://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com\n/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}\n\n**Required scope:**`sfcc.inventory.availability.rw`\n\n### 64-api-endpoints6.4 API Endpoints\n\n| Operation | Method | Endpoint | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Create or update inventory record | `PUT` | `/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}` | Full replace of record |\n| Partial update inventory record | `PATCH` | `/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}` | Update specific fields only. Negative allocation amounts are disallowed |\n| Get inventory record | `GET` | `/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}` | Read current record before update if needed |\n| Delete inventory record | `DELETE` | `/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}` | Remove record entirely |\n\n### 65-inventory-record-payload6.5 Inventory Record Payload\n\n`PUT` — full record write:\n\nDefaultjson{\n\"allocation\": 12,\n\"allocationResetDate\": \"2025-07-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\n\"ats\": 12,\n\"onOrder\": 0,\n\"perpetual\": false,\n\"preorderable\": false,\n\"preorderAllocation\": 0,\n\"backorderable\": false,\n\"backorderAllocation\": 0,\n\"stockLevel\": 12\n}\n\n`PATCH` — partial update (quantity only):\n\nDefaultjson{\n\"allocation\": 8,\n\"ats\": 8,\n\"stockLevel\": 8\n}\n> **Note:** Negative allocation amounts are explicitly disallowed by the SCAPI Inventory Lists API — MuleSoft must validate that no negative values are sent.\n\n### 66-persite-inventory-lists6.6 Per-Site Inventory Lists\n\n| Site | Inventory List ID | Sync Region |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `inventory_m_au` | AU |\n| ZimmermannUK | `inventory_m_uk` | GB |\n| ZimmermannUS | `inventory_m_us` | US |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | `inventory_m_us` | US (shared pool) |\n| ZimmermannEU | `inventory_m_eu` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | `inventory_m_eu_intl` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannHK | `inventory_m_hk` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannME | `inventory_m_me` | TBC |\n\n### 67-put-vs-patch6.7 PUT vs PATCH\n\nUse `PUT` for a full inventory record write from NewStore (all fields known). Use `PATCH` only for targeted partial corrections (e.g. adjusting `allocation` only after a manual stock adjustment). For the standard 15-minute NewStore sync, `PUT` is the correct method.\n\n---\n\n7-rate-limits-and-throttling7. Rate Limits and Throttling\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Concern | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Rate limit | SCAPI Admin API: requests per minute per client — confirm exact limit with Salesforce TAM |\n| Timeout | SCAPI Admin API: 60-second response timeout per call |\n| 429 response | Back off — exponential back-off starting at 5 seconds; retry |\n| Parallel calls | Parallelise per domain within rate limit — use Anypoint throttling policy |\n| Bulk endpoint | No native bulk endpoint for products or inventory records — each is a separate call |\n| Recommended rate | 10 requests/second via Anypoint rate limiting; monitor 429 responses in Anypoint |\n\n---\n\n8-error-handling8. Error Handling\n---------------------------------\n\n| Scenario | Handling |\n| --- | --- |\n| 404 on product existence check | Product does not exist — switch to POST. Not an error |\n| 400 Bad Request | Invalid payload — log record ID and error detail; skip; continue; alert on post-run summary |\n| 409 Conflict | Concurrent write conflict — retry once after 2-second delay |\n| 422 Unprocessable Entity | Business validation failure (e.g. master missing for variant, negative inventory) — log and skip |\n| 429 Rate Limited | Exponential back-off: 5s, 10s, 20s; alert if persistent |\n| 500 / 503 Server Error | Retry up to 3 times; move to failed queue; alert |\n| Token expired | Re-acquire AmOAuth2 token mid-batch; cache and refresh proactively before TTL |\n| Negative inventory value | MuleSoft must validate and reject before calling API — negative allocations are disallowed |\n| Partial batch failure | Log all failed record IDs; raise Anypoint alert; store for replay |\n\n---\n\n9-operational-comparison-vs-filebased9. Operational Comparison vs File-Based\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Aspect | File-Based (WebDAV + Import Job) | SCAPI Admin API |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Bulk catalogue load | ✅ Single zip | ❌ Thousands of calls |\n| Real-time single product | ❌ Minutes latency | ✅ Seconds |\n| Rate limits | ✅ None on import job | ❌ Rate limited |\n| Sequencing | ✅ Handled by job | ❌ MuleSoft must enforce |\n| Upsert support (product) | ✅ Merge mode native | ❌ GET + POST/PUT per record |\n| Inventory write | ✅ XML import | ✅ SCAPI Inventory Lists API (`PUT`/`PATCH`) |\n| Negative inventory guard | ✅ Handled by import job | ❌ MuleSoft must validate before call |\n| Error visibility | ✅ BM log (job-level + record-level) | ✅ Per-call HTTP response |\n| MuleSoft dev effort | Low | High |\n| Price sync | ✅ Pricebook XML import | ❌ **No API exists — must use file-based regardless** |\n| Fit for Zimmermann scale | ✅ Recommended | ⚠ Product/inventory supplement only — price always file-based |\n\n---\n\n10-sync-flow-diagram10. Sync Flow Diagram\n-----------------------------------------\n\n> **Diagram placeholder**\n>\n> *Rovo prompt: Create a swim-lane sequence diagram titled \"MuleSoft → SFCC Catalogue Sync — SCAPI Admin API Pattern (Hybrid)\". Five vertical swim lanes labelled: \"AP21 / NewStore\", \"MuleSoft\", \"SCAPI Admin API\", \"SFCC WebDAV + Import Job\", \"SFCC Catalogue\". Show the following sequence across three colour-coded flows: Product (blue) — MuleSoft acquires AmOAuth2 token → GET existence check → POST create or PUT update master → POST/PUT each variant → PUT category assignment → each SCAPI call returns 200/201 or error; Inventory (orange) — MuleSoft PUT /inventory/v1/.../inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId} per variant per inventory list via SCAPI Inventory Lists Admin API; Price (green) — MuleSoft generates pricebook XML zip → PUT to WebDAV → POST SCAPI Jobs Admin API to trigger sfcc-site-archive-import → poll status → archive or fail. Show a clear visual callout on the Price lane: \"No SCAPI Admin API — file-based only\". Show sequencing dependency arrows: master must exist before variant; variant must exist before inventory. Use Zimmermann brand palette — neutral background, clear typography.*\n\n---\n\n11-open-items11. Open Items\n---------------------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm SCAPI Admin API rate limits per environment (sandbox / staging / production) — required to configure MuleSoft Anypoint throttling policy | Integration Lead / Salesforce TAM | Open |\n| 2 | Confirm whether SCAPI Products Admin API supports bulk/batch product operations — if available, this significantly reduces call volume | Integration Lead / SFCC Architect | Open |\n| 3 | Confirm inventory sync region coverage for EU, EUIntl, HK, ME | Integration Lead / Platform team | Open |\n| 4 | Confirm Account Manager OAuth2 client registration and required scopes (`sfcc.inventory.availability.rw` + product scopes) for MuleSoft across sandbox, staging, and production | Integration Lead / SFCC Admin | Open |\n| 5 | Confirm MuleSoft Anypoint MQ strategy for sequencing (master → variant → inventory) — queue-based vs sequential flow | MuleSoft Architect | Open |\n| 6 | Confirm with Salesforce TAM whether a SCAPI Admin API for pricebook entry writes is on the roadmap — if released this would allow a fully API-based pattern | Integration Lead / Salesforce TAM | Open |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f50c",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

