      "value": "> **DRAFT: for squad review, not final.** Restructured into the Zimmermann TSD template (v0.2). One area remains open pending Victor Crisostomo (SFCC-121): the current runtime state of the `bkzk-002` sandbox (see Sections 2.2 and 7). Not approved for implementation until the Section 8 sign-off is completed by the Technical Lead.\n\nDocument Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-122 |\n| **Author(s)** | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A / FED Lead |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | Technical Lead (to be confirmed) |\n| **Created** | 22 Jul 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.2, Draft |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-122 |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 22 Jul 2026 | Initial spike inventory (pre-template): SCAPI-via-MRT capabilities for product, category, pricing | Angelo Navarro |\n| v0.2 | 23 Jul 2026 | Restructured into the TSD template; folded in verified Confluence findings; \"MRT API\" scope clarified (Admin API vs SCAPI); source citations added to Sections 3 and 4 | Angelo Navarro |\n\n---\n\n1. Problem Statement\n--------------------\n\n### 1.1 Context\n\nThe Zimmermann storefront is a PWA Kit application on Managed Runtime (MRT) that consumes commerce data from SFCC. Building and testing the storefront (product listing, product detail, pricing) in the lower environments requires product, category, and pricing data to be available through the APIs the storefront calls.\n\n### 1.2 Problem\n\nProduct and price data are absent from the lower environments because the source-to-SFCC feeds are not built yet (catalogue: AP21 to MuleSoft to SFCC; price: AP21 to SFCC). Compounding this, \"SFCC MRT API capabilities\" is ambiguous across the squad: it is unclear what Managed Runtime itself provides versus what the storefront consumes. Without a clear, documented picture of the available APIs and a way to populate data, front-end build and test are blocked.\n\n### 1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\nSquad-A cannot build or test product listing, product detail, or pricing against real data. Work either stalls or proceeds against mocks that drift from the real SCAPI responses, creating rework and schedule risk, while the team waits on the MuleSoft integration (SFCC-121) with no interim path.\n\n### 1.4 Success Criteria\n\n* A documented inventory of the SFCC APIs available through MRT for product, category, and pricing (endpoints, authentication, payload).\n* A confirmed, repeatable way to populate the `bkzk-002` sandbox so `shopper-products`, `shopper-search`, and pricing return data.\n* Front-end can consume product, category, and price via SCAPI in a lower environment with no code change once data exists.\n* A clear separation of permanent architecture versus interim workaround.\n\n---\n\n2. Constraints & Assumptions\n----------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Platform | SFCC B2C Commerce + PWA Kit on MRT. No alternative platform is in scope. |\n| Integration layer | Catalogue, price, order, and stock data reach SFCC through MuleSoft or server-side feeds. The PWA does not call AP21 or other back-office systems directly. |\n| Data consumption | The storefront reads commerce data only via SCAPI Shopper APIs through the MRT proxy; it does not write catalogue or price data. |\n| Storefront scope | Must work across all Zimmermann storefronts (10 PWA sites over 7 SFCC sites). No single-market workaround. |\n\n### 2.2 Assumptions\n\n| Assumption | Risk if Wrong |\n| --- | --- |\n| SCAPI can serve product, category, and pricing once data exists (verified against the codebase). | If wrong, the block is an API gap, not just data. Verified, so low risk. |\n| The `bkzk-002` sandbox can be populated now via a `data/core` import plus a manual sample-data load, independent of MuleSoft. | If wrong (no sample data, or no access), the interim unblock fails and the team must wait for the MuleSoft feed. To confirm with Victor. |\n| First-time BM setup (storefront-catalogue assignment, search-index rebuild) can be completed on the sandbox. | If incomplete, `shopper-search` returns nothing even with a catalogue loaded. To confirm with Victor. |\n| Front-end has, or can obtain, access to run the load, or platform runs it on request. | If wrong, the team cannot self-serve the interim load. To confirm with Victor. |\n\n---\n\n3. Options Analysis\n-------------------\n\nThe sub-problem: how do we get product, category, and price data into the lower environments so the squad can build now, before the MuleSoft feed exists?\n\n**Sources.** Options A and B, and the preference for A over B, are taken from Confluence \"TSD: Catalogue Sync, SCAPI Admin API Design (Alternative Pattern)\" (315490342) and its parent file-based design (312508418), which name file-based import as the recommended approach for Zimmermann's catalogue scale and the SCAPI Admin API as the alternative. Those pages describe the permanent MuleSoft to SFCC sync; the same mechanisms are applied here to the interim sample load (see Section 4.2). Option C is the status-quo baseline, included for completeness and not drawn from a source document.\n\n### 3.1 Options Summary\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Viable? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Option A: File-based import** (WebDAV + `sfcc-site-archive-import`) of the `data/core` structure plus `data/sample` data | + Recommended by Confluence for catalogue scale + Single repeatable bulk load; handles sequencing + Only pattern that also loads price (pricebook XML) | - Needs sandbox/WebDAV access and someone to run it - Sample data is not production-representative | Yes |\n| **Option B: SCAPI Admin API** per record (Products + Inventory Lists, AmOAuth2) | + Real-time per product; no file staging | - Thousands of calls for bulk; rate-limited; caller must enforce sequencing - No pricebook write API, so price still needs file-based | Supplementary only |\n| **Option C: Wait for the MuleSoft feed** (no interim load) | + No interim throwaway work | - Blocks front-end build/test until SFCC-121 lands; timeline unknown | No |\n\n### 3.2 Option Detail\n\n#### Option A: File-based import\n\nApply the source-controlled structure (`npm run data:import:core` / `sfcc-ci instance:import`), then load a filtered sample catalogue from `data/sample/` and pricebook XML via WebDAV plus the `sfcc-site-archive-import` job. This is Confluence's recommended pattern for Zimmermann's catalogue scale and is the only pattern that can load price data. Source: Confluence 315490342 (Context callout and Section 9) and 312508418.\n\n#### Option B: SCAPI Admin API (supplementary)\n\nMuleSoft (or a script) calls the SCAPI Products and Inventory Lists Admin APIs per record, authenticated via Account Manager OAuth2. Suited to real-time single-product updates, not bulk load, and it cannot write pricebooks. Useful later for deltas; not the interim unblock. Source: Confluence 315490342 (Sections 4, 6, and 9).\n\n#### Option C: Wait for MuleSoft *(Discarded)*\n\nDiscarded: it leaves the front-end blocked for an unknown period (dependency on SFCC-121) when an interim load is available. Baseline option; no source document.\n\n---\n\n4. Recommended Option & Rationale\n---------------------------------\n\n### 4.1 Recommended Option\n\n**Option A: File-based import of the** `data/core` **structure plus** `data/sample` **sample data.**\n\n### 4.2 Rationale\n\nOption A matches the Confluence-recommended pattern for catalogue scale (per \"TSD: Catalogue Sync\", 315490342 Section 9 and its parent 312508418), is a single repeatable load, and is the only option that also populates price (per 315490342 Section 5: no pricebook write API exists). It unblocks front-end build and test with no code change and is independent of the MuleSoft feed timeline. Option B is retained only as a supplementary, real-time mechanism; Option C blocks the squad.\n\nNote: the Confluence recommendation is written for the permanent MuleSoft to SFCC sync. The same load mechanism (WebDAV + `sfcc-site-archive-import`) applies here to the interim sample load, so the recommendation carries over; framing it as the interim unblock is this TSD's extension, not a verbatim Confluence recommendation.\n\n### 4.3 Trade-offs Accepted\n\nThe interim sample load is throwaway once the permanent AP21-to-MuleSoft-to-SFCC feed is delivering. It depends on sandbox/WebDAV access and someone running the import (a dependency on platform / Victor), and the sample data is not production-representative.\n\n---\n\n5. Technical Implementation\n---------------------------\n\n### 5.1 High-Level Sequence\n\n1. Apply the source-controlled structure: `npm run data:import:core` (`sfcc-ci instance:import`) loads the catalogues (`zimmermann-catalog`, `zimmermann-<site>-storefront-catalog`) and the empty pricebook and inventory shells. Safe to re-run.\n2. Load sample product data: import the filtered sample catalogue from `data/sample/` (manual, for dev and demo).\n3. Load sample prices: deliver Pricebook XML via WebDAV and run the `sfcc-site-archive-import` job. IDs follow `{site}-{currency}-list-prices` / `-sale-prices`.\n4. Complete first-time BM setup: storefront-catalogue assignment per site, pricebook assignment, and a search-index rebuild.\n5. Verify: obtain a SLAS guest token and run a `shopper-search` call for a known category. If it returns zero results, rebuild the search index (step 4) and retry.\n6. Front-end consumes product, category, and price via `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` hooks. No code change is required.\n\n### 5.2 Component / API Changes\n\n| File / Endpoint | Change Required | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `sfccworkplace` `data/core` import | Apply catalogues + pricebook/inventory shells to the sandbox | Config (existing tooling) |\n| `sfccworkplace` `data/sample` import | Manually load sample products for dev/demo | Config |\n| Pricebook XML via WebDAV + `sfcc-site-archive-import` | Load sample prices | Config |\n| Business Manager first-time setup | Catalogue assignment, pricebook assignment, search-index rebuild | Config |\n| PWA `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` hooks | None; the storefront already consumes SCAPI | No change |\n\n### 5.3 Data Structures / Interfaces\n\nThe storefront consumes SCAPI Shopper APIs through the MRT proxy path `/mobify/proxy/api` (`config/default.js:131`), base host `{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com` (Dev: `qmyt7hks...`), SLAS private-client auth. Params: `clientId`, `organizationId` (`f_ecom_bkzk_002`), `shortCode` (`qmyt7hks`), `siteId` (`ZimmermannAU` default).\n\n| API family | Path root | Serves | Verbs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Shopper Products | `/product/shopper-products/v1/*` | Product detail, master/variant, images, prices | GET |\n| Shopper Search | `/search/shopper-search/v1/*` | Category listing (`cgid`), search, faceting, sort | GET |\n| Shopper Promotions | `/pricing/shopper-promotions/v1/*` | Active promotions, coupon validation | GET |\n| Shopper Login (SLAS) | `/checkout/shopper-login/oauth2/*` | Guest and registered auth, token lifecycle | GET, POST |\n| Shopper Baskets | `/checkout/shopper-baskets/v2/*` | Basket / cart lifecycle | GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE |\n| Shopper Orders | `/checkout/shopper-orders/v1/*` | Placement and lookup of the just-placed order (order history is via MuleSoft) | POST, GET |\n| Shopper Customers | `/customer/shopper-customers/v1/*` | Profile, addresses, saved-payment references | GET, POST, PATCH |\n\nCanonical product/category/pricing query (proven in `overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx:52-58`):\n\n`useProductSearch({\nparameters: {\nrefine: [\"cgid=<categoryId>\", \"htype=master\"],\nexpand: [\"promotions\", \"variations\", \"prices\", \"images\", \"custom_properties\"],\nperPricebook: true,\nallVariationProperties: true\n}\n})`\n\nOut of scope for this problem, documented for completeness: OCAPI via `/mobify/proxy/ocapi` (configured, not called from app code); MuleSoft direct reads via `/mobify/proxy/mulesoft` (orders, returns, boutique stock only, not yet wired); Einstein recommendations; and the Managed Runtime Admin API (`mrt-admin`), which administers environments, bundles, and proxies and is platform / CI-CD, not commerce data.\n\n### 5.4 Error Handling & Edge Cases\n\n| Scenario | Expected Behaviour | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `shopper-search` returns zero results after a catalogue load | Search index not rebuilt; rebuild it in BM, then results appear | Edge case |\n| Prices do not render on PDP/PLP | Pricebook not loaded or not assigned to the site; load pricebook XML and assign | Edge case |\n| SLAS guest token / session fails on MRT | Server-Side Cookie Access (`allow_cookies`) is off on the environment; enable it | Error |\n| SCAPI 5xx on catalogue read | `commerce-sdk-react` retries with backoff; show cached data or an error state | Error |\n\n### 5.5 Configuration & Environment Notes\n\n* **Commerce API params:** `config/default.js:130-138` (env-injected). **Proxies:** `config/default.js:208-217` (`api` to SCAPI, `ocapi` to sandbox). **SLAS private client:** `overrides/app/ssr.js:52`.\n* **Per-environment config:** `config/{dev,test,sit,staging,uat,production}.js`; switch with `npm run env -- <tier>`; deploy with `npm run push:<tier>` (`pwa-kit-dev push -t <target>`). MRT environment variables are managed in the Runtime Admin console / Admin API and rotated independently of the codebase.\n* **MRT platform constraints** (official docs): render timeout 20s prod / 16s non-prod; request/response 6 MB; cookies off by default (enable `allow_cookies`); reserved `/mobify` path prefix; `ap-southeast-2` (Sydney) is a supported region.\n* **Current sandbox configuration state is unconfirmed** (whether structure and data are loaded, and whether BM first-time setup is complete); this is an open item for Victor (Section 7).\n\n---\n\n6. Testing & Validation\n-----------------------\n\n### 6.1 Test Coverage\n\n| Test Type | What is Being Tested | Pass Criteria |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Integration | SCAPI reachability from the sandbox (SLAS guest token to `shopper-search`) | Returns more than zero products for a known `cgid` |\n| Integration | Pricing via `expand=prices`, `perPricebook=true` | Product returns list and sale price from the assigned pricebook |\n| E2E / Playwright (@p0) | PLP and PDP render against sandbox data | Category page lists products; PDP shows price and images |\n| Unit | `commerce-sdk-react` hooks consume the responses | Hooks return typed product / search results |\n\n### 6.2 Regression Risk\n\nLow. This work loads data into a lower-environment sandbox and documents the consumption path; it changes no production application code. The PWA already consumes SCAPI, so populating data does not alter app logic. Guard: ensure sample data is not promoted to higher environments.\n\n---\n\n7. Risks & Mitigations\n----------------------\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Current `bkzk-002` data state unknown; may be empty | Med | Confirm with Victor; run `data:import:core` + sample load if needed | Victor (SFCC-121) |\n| No usable sample dataset, or no access to run the load | Med | Confirm sample data exists; obtain sandbox / WebDAV / `sfcc-ci` access | Victor / Platform |\n| Search index not rebuilt, so `shopper-search` is empty | Med | Rebuild index during BM first-time setup; verify via smoke test | Platform / Front-end |\n| MuleSoft catalogue/price feed timeline unknown (SFCC-121) | High | Interim sample load carries build and test until the feed lands | Victor (SFCC-121) |\n| Cookies off by default on MRT breaks the SLAS refresh flow | Low | Enable Server-Side Cookie Access (`allow_cookies`) per environment | Platform |\n| MuleSoft real-time rate limits unconfirmed (direct-read path) | Low | Not needed for product/price; confirm before wiring order/stock reads | Integration Lead |\n\n---\n\n8. Decision Record\n------------------\n\n| Date | Decision Maker | Decision | Outcome / Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 22 Jul | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A | Reached out to Mani (SFCC-1) for direction and any existing documentation on SFCC-122 | Confirm what is already documented before producing new material |\n| 22 Jul | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A | Scope \"MRT API\" to the data-consumption reading (SCAPI via the MRT proxy); the MRT Admin API is out of scope | Ticket objective is product, pricing, and category data consumption |\n| 22-23 Jul | M. Ramachandran (Mani), SFCC-1 | Directed the work to the existing Confluence documentation and to Victor for the current sandbox state | Most of the information is already documented |\n| 23 Jul | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A | Interim unblock is a file-based sample load; SCAPI Admin API is supplementary; price is always file-based | Per Confluence Catalogue Sync TSDs; no pricebook write API exists |\n| 23 Jul | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A | Drafted this TSD; routed the open items (Sections 2.2, 7) to Victor for review and resolution | Open items are operational and current-state; owned by Victor (SFCC-121); awaiting his input |\n| TBC | Technical Lead | TSD approved for implementation | Pending Victor's resolution, then Technical Lead review |\n\n### Sign-off\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Angelo Navarro | 23 Jul 2026 | Submitted |\n| Technical Lead / Reviewer | To be confirmed | Pending | Changes Required |\n\n---\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n* Codebase (`zimmermann-pwa`): `.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md`, `03-mulesoft.md`; `config/default.js`, `config/sites.overlay.js`; `overrides/app/ssr.js`, `.../components/_app-config/index.tsx`, `.../pages/home/index.tsx`, `.../ssr/connectionPools.ts`; `package.json`.\n* Confluence (space SFCC): Business Manager Configuration Management (309657601); TSD Catalogue Sync file-based (312508418) and SCAPI Admin API alternative (315490342); TSD Product (292061208); TSD Price (292388871); TSD PWA (256835585); BM Guides \"Catalog & Product Setup\" (339836968) and \"Price Books\" (340000816); MuleSoft Open Questions (320602113); Build and Deployment, Headless (264896514).\n* Jira (project SFCC): SFCC-122, SFCC-121, SFCC-123, SFCC-1.\n* Official Salesforce docs: Managed Runtime Overview and Administration (including the `mrt-admin` API reference).",
